# Response headers for the landing page (Cloudflare Pages project "extrudo-site",
# ADR-0057). Stricter than the app's: no WASM, so no 'unsafe-eval' or
# 'wasm-unsafe-eval', and no cross-origin isolation needed. Rules are additive
# (see apps/web/public/_headers), so Cache-Control sits in rules that never overlap.
#
# The two Cloudflare hosts in the policy are Cloudflare Web Analytics, which Pages
# injects before </body> when it is enabled for the project (Metrics > Web
# Analytics, ADR-0057 amendment): the beacon is a script from
# static.cloudflareinsights.com and reports to cloudflareinsights.com. The app's
# policy has no analytics and neither host.

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=(), usb=()
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' https://static.cloudflareinsights.com; style-src 'self'; img-src 'self' data:; media-src 'self'; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self' https://cloudflareinsights.com; manifest-src 'self'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'

/
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/index.html
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/sw.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache

/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
